macOS: reject provably unavailable single waits through a pinned snapshot.

Cider-Topic: sync/msync
Cider-Requires: 0105-msync-co-locate-thread-local-state.patch
Cider-Status: nondefault candidate; performance/continuous gates separate
Cider-Test: production-header snapshot guards and four rejected negative controls;
 PE32/64 functionality, lifecycle and actual cross-process runtime in owned lab
Cider-Review-By: independent scoped read-only concurrency review and parent

Successful acquisitions and every mutation still use the original transaction.
The read-only probe admits only one nonalertable auto-event or semaphore with
zero availability, a live pinned native frame and matching even TID epoch.
SC owner/version observations, atomic64 payload and a real thread fence reject
interference; pending journals take normal recovery. The existing compare-before-
park path and timeout semantics remain. Advance shared magic to4 and load only
matching client/server components. Allocation/reuse is excluded by the existing
exported shared reference held by the native frame.

